# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed variables to
# the app, and inlines them at BUILD time — a production build carries whatever
# was set when it was built, so rebuild after changing any of these.

# ── Mocking ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When true (the default), Mock Service Worker intercepts every request and the
# three URLs below are never actually contacted. Set to false to hit the real
# service. Leaving it unset means mocked, on purpose: an accidental real
# submission to a government service is much worse than an accidental mock.
VITE_USE_MOCK=true

# ── Endpoints ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Relative paths are resolved against the app's own origin, which is what you
# want when routing through the Vite dev proxy (see vite.config.ts) to dodge
# CORS. Absolute https:// URLs also work if the service sends CORS headers.

# GET {VITE_LOOKUP_URL}?numprotocol=<15 digits>  ->  { "id": "..." }
# Runs once per scan, right after you confirm it.
VITE_LOOKUP_URL=/api/protocols

# GET {VITE_PROTOCOL_URL}/<id>
# The ordinary protocol submission.
VITE_PROTOCOL_URL=/api/protocols

# GET {VITE_PROTOCOL_AS_URL}/<id>
# The AS submission — a separate service. Only ever called after the ordinary
# protocol above has succeeded for the same id; AS alone is never valid.
VITE_PROTOCOL_AS_URL=/api/protocols-as

# ── Misc ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-request timeout in milliseconds.
VITE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
